// elimination_coarse_chain.vo.expected: expected VO derived by hand from doc/formal (ir_vo.tex WF-VO-*,
// passes.tex I1-I5 and the planner O-/S-/R- rules), independently of the producer.
// Every step is preceded by the rule that fixes its position; RULE GAP marks a position the rules leave open,
// with the tie-break used.
// Planner elimination,coarse.
// c0=Edge(a,b), c1=Edge(b,c), c2=Edge(d,c)
// RULE GAP (elimination order): passes.tex:333-334 says only "reverse maximum-cardinality search on the primal
// graph, with connected-ready variables or binders first"; the MCS start vertex and tie-break are unstated.
// Derivation assumes MCS ties broken by first written occurrence of the variable; this is an assumption, not a
// rule.
// MCS from a: a,b,c,d; E=[d,c,b,a]; e_0=2, e_1=1, e_2=0.
struct OrientedChain ; relation Edge (src : i32 [0] , dst : i32 [0]) ; answer (a , d) : - Edge (a , b) , Edge (b , c) , Edge (d , c) ;
valuation {
    // B={}: least e_i = 0 -> c2
    Edge @ 2 (d , c) ;
    // B={c,d}: c1 connected (c), c0 disconnected -> c1
    Edge @ 1 (b , c) ;
    // c0 connected via b; last
    Edge @ 0 (a , b) ;
}
